; A FLOAT `.size` operand. A size counts whole bytes, so the operand is refused gracefully rather
; than cast through a saturating `as i128` (which once truncated `1.5` to 1 here, and turned
; `(-1.0e300..1.0e300)` into `pub type X = f32;`). The integral-float and member-route siblings
; are pinned by `robustness_tests::size_float_operand_rejects_gracefully`.
x = bytes .size (1.5..2)
